      "source": [
        "## Step 16 — Cross-station synchrony: do stations move together?\n",
        "\n",
        "This is a core analysis for the project question. For each pollutant, we compare stations on the same dates. We use supported records (12+ readings), apply `log1p` to non-negative concentrations, and subtract each station’s monthly median log concentration before computing pairwise Spearman correlations. This reduces persistent station-level differences and broad monthly level shifts. Each station pair must have at least 30 overlapping dates. The resulting correlations describe co-movement, not causation or proof of a shared source."
      ]
    },
