        "## Step 17 — Station-relative unusual observations and multi-station co-occurrence\n",
        "\n",
        "To avoid imposing one concentration threshold across all stations, we flag observations above each station’s own 95th percentile for that pollutant, calculated using supported records. These are **statistical upper-tail flags**, not regulatory exceedances and not confirmed pollution events. The 95th-percentile cut-offs use the full observed period for descriptive EDA only; if these labels are used in a formal predictive test, re-estimate thresholds on training data only. For each date, we count how many reporting stations are flagged. A date is labelled `multi_station_cooccurrence` only when at least three stations report and at least 25% of the reporting stations are flagged. This is a descriptive screening rule; the exported sensitivity table also checks 20% and 33% shares."
      ]
